---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NavBar from '../components/Navigation/NavBar';
import FooterSection from '../components/Footer/FooterSection';
import '../components/Privacy/privacy.scss';
---

<BaseLayout
  pathname="/privacy"
  title="Privacy | Casey Key"
  description="How this site handles visit data for the live Ops Pulse telemetry map."
>
  <NavBar client:load pathname={Astro.url.pathname} />
  <main class="privacy">
    <header class="privacy__header">
      <h1 class="privacy__heading">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="privacy__subheader">
        What the live Ops Pulse map on the home page records, and what it never
        records.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="privacy__body">
      <h2 class="privacy__section-title">What the map shows</h2>
      <p>
        The hero of this site renders a live map of recent visits. Each dot is a
        coarse location cell, roughly the size of a city, and it appears only
        after someone has actually loaded the page.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your own visit is the pulsing marker. Other visitors appear as static
        dots, so you can tell at a glance which one is you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="privacy__section-title">What is recorded</h2>
      <ul class="privacy__list">
        <li>
          <strong>Country</strong> — a two-letter country code, used as a
          fallback position for the dot.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Region and city</strong> — resolved in your own browser from a
          public geolocation service, then rounded to a city-scale cell.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Page path</strong> — the path you loaded, with any query
          string removed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Timing</strong> — when the visit happened and how long the
          page took to respond.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="privacy__section-title">What is never recorded</h2>
      <ul class="privacy__list">
        <li>Your IP address. It is not stored, logged, or sent to the map.</li>
        <li>
          Exact coordinates, an address, or a device identifier. The location
          is rounded to a city-scale cell before it is stored.
        </li>
        <li>
          Cookies, advertising identifiers, or cross-site trackers for this map.
          It uses no storage and no third-party cookies.
        </li>
        <li>
          Referrer hostnames, query strings, or anything identifying you to the
          telemetry service.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="privacy__section-title">How long it is kept</h2>
      <p>
        Detailed city and region information is automatically downgraded to a
        country-level aggregate after 24 hours, and the underlying records are
        deleted within 7 days. The map only ever displays activity from the
        last hour.
      </p>

      <h2 class="privacy__section-title">Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Location is resolved in your browser by a third-party geolocation
        service, which receives your IP address in order to answer the request.
        That service is not operated by this site, and no location data is
        shared with it beyond the lookup itself.
      </p>

      <h2 class="privacy__section-title">Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Something unclear here, or you would like the data for your visits
        removed? <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a> and I will help.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <FooterSection />
</BaseLayout>
